                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is another 'I wish there was a sideways thumb' games.\nThis has a good atmosphere, it's a 'this is too dark' game but they give you a Gamma slider so it isn't a deal breaker.\nSound is well crafted for the most part, doors seem to all have a 'jiggling the door handle' sound effect regardless of whether it has a door handle or not; but that is a minor annoyance.\n\nThe gameplay is hit and miss, you read emails on computer terminals & get directed by a mysterious person texting you & these will direct you to computer passwords, keycodes or items you need to open doors while you gradual uncover spooky evidence about corporations meddling with forces they can't even comprehend & surprise something goes wrong & a fog tries to kill you. Nothing most office workers haven't experience, but it is handled well enough here.\n \nWhen the black fog will chase you, you have to do very trial & error maze running through an office building which to it's credit actually has variety in its corridors, so the problem isn't that it all looks the same, but it feels like the fog is too close, so if you make a wrong turn then you get sucked in & killed & have to do the section over again. It feels like a minor balance issue, because the map is well designed, rather than the annoying same corridor labyrinth trash we've all seen on Steam before.\nThese sections aren't long but they are long enough that you could get killed 5 times before getting the path right.\n\nThat's the only major downfall, it can get frustrating repeating the same section a bunch of times trying to find the right way.\nI'm recommending but it's a cautious one; 'you are locked in a office building' games have been a bit of a gamble as a genre, but this one is better than most unless trial & error really annoys you quickly.",
